\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{Products of separate channels and of their sum}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{In \ref{fdip-018S} take every group action trivial,
#{F=F_\psi=\mathbb C}, and #{Y_0(v)=v\bbI}. On a nonzero
multiplicity space take #{Y_1=Y_2=\bbI_E}. At the scalar
value #{(1,1)}, whose orbit is a single point, each separate
multiplicity product is #{\bbI_E}. The sum of the channels is
#{2\bbI_E} and its product with its adjoint is #{4\bbI_E}.
The sum of the separate products is #{2\bbI_E}. Multiplying the sum by its adjoint also uses both cross terms.}
